            <ArticleTitle>Acute painful diabetic neuropathy following severe weight loss.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>463-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 34-year-old man, recently diagnosed as diabetic, presented an acute painful neuropathy. He reported a profound weight loss during the months preceding onset. There were no motor symptoms, and only mild neurological signs were observed on examination. Improvement was related to a good glycemic control and weight gain. Acute painful diabetic neuropathy is a condition that may affect diabetic patients shortly after development of the disease. The pathogenetic roles played by different factors are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
